 "verdict": {
  "primaryCause": "scorer eligibility gate: a TD can go only to a player with a carry/reception in that world; red-zone shares are unconditional averages, so gating + renormalising double-counts opportunity and moves TD mass from part-time to every-down players (eligible <80% of worlds: predicted 0.084 vs actual 0.107 vs 0.108 ungated; eligible >=95%: 0.385 vs 0.358). Dirichlet kappas under-produce touches (P>=1 carry 0.397 vs 0.435; P>=1 catch 0.643 vs 0.701; QB carry 0.79 vs 0.90).",
  "secondary": [
   "non-offensive other-TD term absent (0.003/player-game, ~0.0004 log loss)",
   "active red-zone shares sum >1 in ~50% of team-games and are renormalised",
   "OTHER bucket takes 5.5% of TDs vs 2.8% actual"
  ],
  "ruledOut": [
   "team TD count dispersion (world mean 2.32 vs 2.36, dispersion 0.83 vs 0.82)",
   "efficiency term (rzTdV1 has none either)"
  ],
  "shared": "QB under-predicted (level rzTdV1 0.81, world 0.73), RB over-predicted (1.12 / 1.10): needs a per-role efficiency term",
  "limits": "On 2022–2025 the registered world misses rzTdV1 by only 0.0003 log loss and ECE 0.022 (< 0.03); the size of the test-window failure is not reproduced without the forbidden look.",
  "fixRequires": "A NEW preregistration (opportunity-weighted scorer selection or eligibility-adjusted shares, realistic touch rates, other-TD term, QB rushing efficiency, share cap) and a fresh FORWARD evaluation: both development windows have now been examined. World TD marginals stay unpublished until then."
